                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{z \in X: f_x(z) \gt 1/2\}
              are disjoint open neighborhoods containing
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              respectively. Hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is Hausdorff.
            %p
              The other direction is the statement of prop.
